<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" ?>
<!--
  ============================================================================
  BANYNOVA — BASE LAYOUT (Blogger Theme Foundation)
  Version 2.0 — rebuilt to comply with BANYNOVA ENGINEERING STANDARDS
  (Parts 1-9 and 12: Core Principles, Blogger XML, HTML, CSS, JavaScript,
  UI Components, Accessibility WCAG 2.2 AA, Performance, SEO, Production
  Checklist).
  ============================================================================
  Governed by Documentation_Governance_v1.0.md, Design_System_v1.0.md, and
  the BANYNOVA ENGINEERING STANDARDS document.

  WHAT THIS FILE IS
  A COMPLETE, standalone Blogger theme file — not a fragment. Exactly one
  b:skin block, a correct html/head/body skeleton, one Header section and
  one Main section using Blogger's own Blog widget, and a Footer section.

  BEFORE YOU TOUCH ANYTHING IN BLOGGER
  1. Theme -> Backup/Restore -> Download theme. Save that file somewhere
     safe. This is the single most important step.
  2. Theme -> Edit HTML -> select all existing content -> delete it ->
     paste this entire file in its place.
  3. Use Preview BEFORE clicking Save — check homepage, a normal post,
     and mobile width.
  4. Only Save once preview looks correct.

  TWO DELIBERATE DEVIATIONS FROM THE STANDARDS DOCUMENT (flagged, not
  silently applied — Part 3 Section 3 asks for <!DOCTYPE html> and
  <html lang="en">):
  - No literal <!DOCTYPE html> is written here. Blogger's rendering engine
    injects the HTML5 doctype into the final output automatically; the
    template source itself is XML compiled by Blogger, not raw HTML sent
    to the browser. Adding a literal doctype before <html> risks an extra,
    non-standard node ahead of the required single root element.
  - <html lang='en'> IS included below (see the html tag) — that part of
    the standard is followed directly, since it carries no such conflict.

  WHAT STILL NEEDS TO BE FILLED IN
  - Replace the favicon href with your real uploaded favicon URL.
  - Replace the og:image / twitter:image placeholder URL with a real
    1200x630 social image (Part 9 Section 10).
  - Replace the placeholder social/GitHub links in the footer.
  - The post template ("post" includable) stays intentionally minimal —
    the Universal Tool Template (Roadmap Step 4) extends it once tool
    pages are being built.
  - FAQPage / BreadcrumbList JSON-LD are intentionally NOT added here —
    Part 9 Section 13 scopes those to tool pages, and structured data
    should never describe content that isn't visibly on the page yet.

  CHANGELOG (v1.0 -> v2.0)
  - New head order matches Part 2 Section 7 exactly (charset, viewport,
    theme-color, color-scheme, canonical, title, description, OG,
    Twitter, icons, structured data, CSS, critical JS).
  - Added color-scheme meta, referrer-policy meta, og:image, og:locale,
    twitter:image/title/description, and Organization / WebSite+
    SearchAction / WebPage JSON-LD (Part 9 Sections 8, 9, 12).
  - Skip link now targets id="main-content" (Part 7 Section 8).
  - New design tokens: header-height, sidebar-width, and a z-index scale
    (dropdown/sticky/modal/tooltip) replacing ad hoc z-index numbers
    (Part 4 Section 4).
  - body transition now animates background-color, not background
    (Part 4 Section 23).
  - Added img { height: auto } and a documented img/picture/svg block
    (Part 4 Section 18).
  - Added ::selection styling (Part 4 Section 32).
  - Logo SVG de-duplicated into one <symbol>, referenced via <use> in
    the header and footer (Part 2 Section 16).
  - Navigation restructured to Tools / Categories / Blog / Resources /
    About per Part 6 Section 5, with aria-current="page" wired in JS.
  - Footer expanded: Quick Links, Legal (Privacy, Terms, Cookies,
    Accessibility), Contact, plus Sitemap/RSS/GitHub — Disclaimer moved
    out of the primary Legal list into the secondary bottom bar
    (Part 6 Section 20).
  - Header scroll handler now wrapped in Banynova.utils.throttle (100ms)
    instead of an unthrottled listener (Part 5 Section 12).
  - JS reorganized under a proper Banynova.navigation module (scroll,
    mobile menu, active-link) matching the Module Architecture in
    Part 5 Section 4, still frozen per-module (not at the top level) so
    future modules — search, clipboard, etc. — can still be added.
  - Added Banynova.perf.applyLazyLoadingToPostImages(), since Blogger
    post-body <img> tags come from user content and can't be templated
    directly — this is the practical way to apply Part 2 Section 15's
    loading="lazy" / decoding="async" rule to that content, skipping the
    first image so a genuine hero/LCP image is never lazy-loaded.
  - Fixed two non-mobile-first breakpoints (Part 4 Section 11 requires
    mobile-first): h1 size, .bn-section padding, and .bn-footer-grid
    column count now define their small/mobile value as the base rule,
    scaling up via min-width media queries — previously the base rules
    held desktop values overridden down via max-width, which is the
    opposite of mobile-first.
  ============================================================================
-->
<html b:css='false' b:defaultwidgetversion='2' b:layoutsVersion='3' b:responsive='true' expr:dir='data:blog.languageDirection' lang='en' xmlns='http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml' xmlns:b='http://www.google.com/2005/gml/b' xmlns:data='http://www.google.com/2005/gml/data' xmlns:expr='http://www.google.com/2005/gml/expr'>
<head>
<!-- ======================= 1. CHARSET / VIEWPORT ======================= -->
<meta charset='UTF-8'/>
<meta content='width=device-width, initial-scale=1' name='viewport'/>

<!-- ======================= 2. THEME COLOR / COLOR SCHEME ======================= -->
<meta content='#2a6df4' name='theme-color'/>
<meta content='light dark' name='color-scheme'/>

<!-- ======================= 3. CANONICAL ======================= -->
<b:if cond='data:blog.url == data:blog.homepageUrl'>
<link expr:href='data:blog.homepageUrl' rel='canonical'/>
<b:else/>
<link expr:href='data:blog.canonicalUrl' rel='canonical'/>
</b:if>

<!-- ======================= 4. TITLE ======================= -->
<title><data:blog.pageTitle/></title>

<!-- ======================= 5. META DESCRIPTION / ROBOTS / AUTHOR ======================= -->
<!-- Fallback text is the approved sitewide description from the Brand Voice
     Guide — used whenever a page has no custom description set (label
     pages, some posts), so every page still gets a real snippet instead of
     Google auto-generating one from arbitrary page text. -->
<b:if cond='data:blog.metaDescription'>
<meta expr:content='data:blog.metaDescription' name='description'/>
<b:else/>
<meta content='Banynova offers free online tools for developers, marketers, creators, and students. Fast, private, browser-based utilities. No sign-up. No uploads.' name='description'/>
</b:if>
<b:if cond='data:blog.searchLabel OR data:blog.searchQuery'>
<meta content='noindex, follow' name='robots'/>
<b:else/>
<meta content='index, follow' name='robots'/>
</b:if>
<meta content='Banynova' name='author'/>
<meta content='strict-origin-when-cross-origin' name='referrer'/>

<!-- ======================= 6. OPEN GRAPH ======================= -->
<meta content='website' property='og:type'/>
<meta expr:content='data:blog.title' property='og:site_name'/>
<meta expr:content='data:blog.pageName' property='og:title'/>
<meta expr:content='data:blog.canonicalUrl' property='og:url'/>
<b:if cond='data:blog.metaDescription'>
<meta expr:content='data:blog.metaDescription' property='og:description'/>
<b:else/>
<meta content='Banynova offers free online tools for developers, marketers, creators, and students. Fast, private, browser-based utilities. No sign-up. No uploads.' property='og:description'/>
</b:if>
<meta content='https://banynova.blogspot.com/og-image.png' property='og:image'/>
<meta content='en_US' property='og:locale'/>

<!-- ======================= 7. TWITTER CARDS ======================= -->
<meta content='summary_large_image' name='twitter:card'/>
<meta expr:content='data:blog.pageName' name='twitter:title'/>
<b:if cond='data:blog.metaDescription'>
<meta expr:content='data:blog.metaDescription' name='twitter:description'/>
<b:else/>
<meta content='Banynova offers free online tools for developers, marketers, creators, and students. Fast, private, browser-based utilities. No sign-up. No uploads.' name='twitter:description'/>
</b:if>
<meta content='https://banynova.blogspot.com/og-image.png' name='twitter:image'/>

<!-- ======================= 8. ICONS (replace with your uploaded favicon URL) ======================= -->
<link href='https://banynova.blogspot.com/favicon.ico' rel='icon' type='image/x-icon'/>

<!-- ======================= 9. STRUCTURED DATA (JSON-LD) ======================= -->
<script type='application/ld+json'>
{
  &quot;@context&quot;: &quot;https://schema.org&quot;,
  &quot;@type&quot;: &quot;Organization&quot;,
  &quot;name&quot;: &quot;Banynova&quot;,
  &quot;url&quot;: &quot;<data:blog.homepageUrl/>&quot;,
  &quot;slogan&quot;: &quot;Powering Your Digital Workflow.&quot;
}
</script>
<script type='application/ld+json'>
{
  &quot;@context&quot;: &quot;https://schema.org&quot;,
  &quot;@type&quot;: &quot;WebSite&quot;,
  &quot;name&quot;: &quot;<data:blog.title/>&quot;,
  &quot;url&quot;: &quot;<data:blog.homepageUrl/>&quot;,
  &quot;potentialAction&quot;: {
    &quot;@type&quot;: &quot;SearchAction&quot;,
    &quot;target&quot;: &quot;<data:blog.homepageUrl/>search?q={search_term_string}&quot;,
    &quot;query-input&quot;: &quot;required name=search_term_string&quot;
  }
}
</script>
<script type='application/ld+json'>
{
  &quot;@context&quot;: &quot;https://schema.org&quot;,
  &quot;@type&quot;: &quot;WebPage&quot;,
  &quot;name&quot;: &quot;<data:blog.pageTitle/>&quot;,
  &quot;url&quot;: &quot;<data:blog.canonicalUrl/>&quot;,
  &quot;isPartOf&quot;: { &quot;@type&quot;: &quot;WebSite&quot;, &quot;url&quot;: &quot;<data:blog.homepageUrl/>&quot; }
}
</script>

<!-- ======================= 10. NO-FLASH THEME INIT (critical, runs before CSS paints) ======================= -->
<!-- Applies saved preference (LocalStorage) or system preference to <html> before first paint, per Part 2 Section 17 (prevent FOUC). -->
<script>//<![CDATA[
(function () {
  try {
    var saved = window.localStorage.getItem('bn-theme');
    var prefersDark = window.matchMedia && window.matchMedia('(prefers-color-scheme: dark)').matches;
    var mode = saved || (prefersDark ? 'dark' : 'light');
    document.documentElement.setAttribute('data-theme', mode);
  } catch (e) {
    document.documentElement.setAttribute('data-theme', 'light');
  }
})();
//]]></script>

<!-- Defensive critical CSS, adjacent to the script above (Part 8 Section 11
     treats this as legitimate above-the-fold critical CSS, distinct from
     the main design-system skin below). In this template the full skin is
     inline CDATA right after this, so the practical FOUC window is already
     near-zero — this is belt-and-suspenders: it guarantees the background
     flips the instant data-theme is set, with zero dependency on how much
     of the skin the browser has parsed yet. Kept intentionally to just the
     two background colors, not a duplicate of the token system. -->
<style>
html[data-theme="dark"] { background-color: hsl(222, 47%, 11%); }
html[data-theme="light"] { background-color: hsl(220, 20%, 98%); }
</style>

<b:include data='blog' name='all-head-content'/>

<!-- ======================= 11. THE ONE AND ONLY SKIN (CSS) ======================= -->
<b:skin><![CDATA[

/* ==========================================================================
   1. DESIGN TOKENS — see Design_System_v1.0.md Sections 2-8 (source of truth)
   ========================================================================== */
:root {
  --bn-primary-hsl: 220, 90%, 56%;
  --bn-primary: hsl(var(--bn-primary-hsl));
  --bn-primary-hover: hsl(220, 90%, 48%);
  --bn-primary-active: hsl(220, 90%, 40%);
  --bn-primary-subtle: hsl(220, 90%, 96%);
  --bn-secondary-hsl: 215, 16%, 47%;
  --bn-secondary: hsl(var(--bn-secondary-hsl));
  --bn-secondary-subtle: hsl(215, 16%, 94%);
  --bn-accent-hsl: 262, 83%, 58%;
  --bn-accent: hsl(var(--bn-accent-hsl));
  --bn-success: hsl(142, 71%, 45%);
  --bn-success-subtle: hsl(142, 71%, 95%);
  --bn-warning: hsl(38, 92%, 50%);
  --bn-warning-subtle: hsl(38, 92%, 95%);
  --bn-danger: hsl(354, 70%, 54%);
  --bn-danger-hover: hsl(354, 70%, 45%);
  --bn-danger-subtle: hsl(354, 70%, 95%);
  --bn-info: hsl(199, 89%, 48%);
  --bn-info-subtle: hsl(199, 89%, 95%);

  --bn-bg: hsl(220, 20%, 98%);
  --bn-surface: hsl(0, 0%, 100%);
  --bn-surface-raised: hsl(0, 0%, 100%);
  --bn-border: hsl(220, 13%, 88%);
  --bn-border-strong: hsl(220, 13%, 72%);
  --bn-text-primary: hsl(220, 24%, 12%);
  --bn-text-secondary: hsl(220, 12%, 42%);
  --bn-text-tertiary: hsl(220, 9%, 60%);
  --bn-text-on-primary: hsl(0, 0%, 100%);
  --bn-disabled-bg: hsl(220, 13%, 93%);
  --bn-disabled-text: hsl(220, 9%, 60%);

  --bn-focus-ring: 0 0 0 3px hsla(var(--bn-primary-hsl), 0.35);

  --bn-gradient-primary: linear-gradient(135deg, hsl(220,90%,56%), hsl(262,83%,58%));
  --bn-gradient-subtle: linear-gradient(135deg, hsl(220,90%,97%), hsl(262,83%,97%));
  --bn-glass-bg: hsla(0,0%,100%,0.72);
  --bn-blur-md: 12px;

  --bn-font-sans: system-ui, -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, 'Segoe UI', Roboto, Oxygen, Ubuntu, Cantarell, sans-serif;
  --bn-font-mono: ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, Monaco, Consolas, 'Liberation Mono', 'Courier New', monospace;
  --bn-fs-xs: 0.75rem; --bn-fs-sm: 0.875rem; --bn-fs-base: 1rem; --bn-fs-lg: 1.125rem;
  --bn-fs-xl: 1.25rem; --bn-fs-2xl: 1.5rem; --bn-fs-3xl: 1.875rem; --bn-fs-4xl: 2.25rem; --bn-fs-5xl: 3rem;
  --bn-fw-normal: 400; --bn-fw-medium: 500; --bn-fw-semibold: 600; --bn-fw-bold: 700;
  --bn-lh-tight: 1.2; --bn-lh-snug: 1.375; --bn-lh-base: 1.5; --bn-lh-relaxed: 1.625;

  --bn-space-1: 0.25rem; --bn-space-2: 0.5rem; --bn-space-3: 0.75rem; --bn-space-4: 1rem;
  --bn-space-5: 1.25rem; --bn-space-6: 1.5rem; --bn-space-8: 2rem; --bn-space-10: 2.5rem;
  --bn-space-12: 3rem; --bn-space-16: 4rem; --bn-space-20: 5rem; --bn-space-24: 6rem;

  --bn-radius-sm: 0.25rem; --bn-radius-md: 0.5rem; --bn-radius-lg: 0.75rem; --bn-radius-xl: 1rem; --bn-radius-full: 9999px;

  --bn-shadow-1: 0 1px 2px 0 rgba(0,0,0,.05);
  --bn-shadow-2: 0 4px 6px -1px rgba(0,0,0,.1), 0 2px 4px -1px rgba(0,0,0,.06);
  --bn-shadow-3: 0 10px 15px -3px rgba(0,0,0,.1), 0 4px 6px -2px rgba(0,0,0,.05);
  --bn-shadow-4: 0 20px 25px -5px rgba(0,0,0,.1), 0 10px 10px -5px rgba(0,0,0,.04);

  --bn-container-max: 1280px;
  --bn-content-max: 800px;

  /* Layout tokens (Part 4 Section 4 "Layout Tokens") */
  --bn-header-height: 65px;
  --bn-sidebar-width: 320px;

  /* Z-Index scale (Part 4 Section 4 "Layer Tokens") — avoid arbitrary z-index values */
  --bn-z-dropdown: 100;
  --bn-z-sticky: 200;
  --bn-z-modal: 500;
  --bn-z-tooltip: 600;

  --bn-transition-fast: 150ms cubic-bezier(.4,0,.2,1);
  --bn-transition-base: 250ms cubic-bezier(.4,0,.2,1);
  --bn-transition-slow: 350ms cubic-bezier(.4,0,.2,1);
}

[data-theme="dark"] {
  --bn-bg: hsl(222, 47%, 11%);
  --bn-surface: hsl(217, 33%, 17%);
  --bn-surface-raised: hsl(217, 33%, 22%);
  --bn-border: hsl(215, 25%, 27%);
  --bn-border-strong: hsl(215, 20%, 45%);
  --bn-text-primary: hsl(210, 40%, 98%);
  --bn-text-secondary: hsl(215, 20%, 75%);
  --bn-text-tertiary: hsl(215, 16%, 55%);
  --bn-primary-subtle: hsla(220,90%,56%,.15);
  --bn-secondary-subtle: hsla(215,16%,47%,.15);
  --bn-success-subtle: hsla(142,71%,45%,.15);
  --bn-warning-subtle: hsla(38,92%,50%,.15);
  --bn-danger-subtle: hsla(354,70%,54%,.15);
  --bn-info-subtle: hsla(199,89%,48%,.15);
  --bn-disabled-bg: hsl(217,33%,24%);
  --bn-disabled-text: hsl(215,16%,45%);
  --bn-gradient-subtle: linear-gradient(135deg, hsla(220,90%,56%,.12), hsla(262,83%,58%,.12));
  --bn-glass-bg: hsla(217,33%,17%,.72);
  --bn-shadow-1: 0 1px 2px 0 rgba(0,0,0,.4);
  --bn-shadow-2: 0 4px 6px -1px rgba(0,0,0,.5), 0 2px 4px -1px rgba(0,0,0,.3);
  --bn-shadow-3: 0 10px 15px -3px rgba(0,0,0,.6), 0 4px 6px -2px rgba(0,0,0,.4);
  --bn-shadow-4: 0 20px 25px -5px rgba(0,0,0,.7), 0 10px 10px -5px rgba(0,0,0,.5);
}

/* ==========================================================================
   2. CSS RESET
   ========================================================================== */
*, *::before, *::after { box-sizing: border-box; }
html, body, h1, h2, h3, h4, p, figure, blockquote, dl, dd, ul, ol { margin: 0; }
ul[class], ol[class] { list-style: none; padding: 0; }
html:focus-within { scroll-behavior: smooth; }
body { min-height: 100vh; text-rendering: optimizeSpeed; }
img,
picture,
svg {
  display: block;
  max-width: 100%;
}
img { height: auto; }
input, button, textarea, select { font: inherit; color: inherit; }
a { color: inherit; }
@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
  html:focus-within { scroll-behavior: auto; }
  *, *::before, *::after { animation-duration: 0.01ms !important; animation-iteration-count: 1 !important; transition-duration: 0.01ms !important; scroll-behavior: auto !important; }
}

/* ==========================================================================
   3. BASE ELEMENTS & TYPOGRAPHY
   ========================================================================== */
html { -webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%; }
body {
  font-family: var(--bn-font-sans);
  font-size: var(--bn-fs-base);
  line-height: var(--bn-lh-base);
  color: var(--bn-text-primary);
  background: var(--bn-bg);
  -webkit-font-smoothing: antialiased;
  transition: background-color var(--bn-transition-base), color var(--bn-transition-base);
}
h1, h2, h3, h4 { line-height: var(--bn-lh-tight); font-weight: var(--bn-fw-bold); color: var(--bn-text-primary); }
h1 { font-size: var(--bn-fs-3xl); }
h2 { font-size: var(--bn-fs-3xl); }
h3 { font-size: var(--bn-fs-2xl); }
h4 { font-size: var(--bn-fs-xl); }
p { color: var(--bn-text-secondary); }
a { text-decoration: none; }
code, pre, kbd { font-family: var(--bn-font-mono); }
:focus-visible { outline: none; box-shadow: var(--bn-focus-ring); border-radius: var(--bn-radius-sm); }
::selection { background: var(--bn-primary); color: var(--bn-text-on-primary); }

/* ==========================================================================
   4. LAYOUT SYSTEM
   ========================================================================== */
.bn-container { max-width: var(--bn-container-max); margin-inline: auto; padding-inline: var(--bn-space-6); }
.bn-content { max-width: var(--bn-content-max); margin-inline: auto; }
.bn-section { padding-block: var(--bn-space-12); }
.bn-section--tight { padding-block: var(--bn-space-12); }

.bn-grid { display: grid; gap: var(--bn-space-5); grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(260px, 1fr)); }
.bn-grid--categories { grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(220px, 1fr)); }
.bn-grid--tutorials { grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(280px, 1fr)); }
.bn-grid--stats { grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(160px, 1fr)); }

/* ==========================================================================
   5. COMPONENTS
   ========================================================================== */

/* --- Skip Link --- */
.bn-skip-link {
  position: absolute; top: -48px; left: var(--bn-space-4); z-index: var(--bn-z-tooltip);
  background: var(--bn-primary); color: var(--bn-text-on-primary);
  padding: var(--bn-space-3) var(--bn-space-5); border-radius: var(--bn-radius-md);
  font-weight: var(--bn-fw-semibold); transition: top var(--bn-transition-fast);
}
.bn-skip-link:focus { top: var(--bn-space-4); }

/* --- Header --- */
.bn-header { position: sticky; top: 0; z-index: var(--bn-z-sticky); background: var(--bn-surface); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--bn-border); transition: background-color var(--bn-transition-base), backdrop-filter var(--bn-transition-base); }
.bn-header.is-scrolled { background: var(--bn-glass-bg); backdrop-filter: blur(var(--bn-blur-md)); -webkit-backdrop-filter: blur(var(--bn-blur-md)); }
.bn-header-inner { display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: space-between; gap: var(--bn-space-4); padding-block: var(--bn-space-4); min-height: var(--bn-header-height); }
.bn-logo { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: var(--bn-space-2); font-weight: var(--bn-fw-bold); font-size: var(--bn-fs-xl); color: var(--bn-text-primary); }
.bn-logo-mark { color: var(--bn-primary); }

/* --- Navigation --- */
.bn-nav { display: none; align-items: center; gap: var(--bn-space-6); font-size: var(--bn-fs-sm); font-weight: var(--bn-fw-medium); color: var(--bn-text-secondary); }
@media (min-width: 860px) { .bn-nav { display: flex; } }
.bn-nav a:hover { color: var(--bn-primary); }
.bn-nav a[aria-current="page"] { color: var(--bn-primary); font-weight: var(--bn-fw-semibold); }
.bn-header-actions { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: var(--bn-space-2); }
.bn-icon-btn { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; width: 40px; height: 40px; border-radius: var(--bn-radius-md); border: 1px solid var(--bn-border); background: var(--bn-surface); color: var(--bn-text-secondary); transition: background-color var(--bn-transition-fast), border-color var(--bn-transition-fast); }
.bn-icon-btn:hover { background: var(--bn-primary-subtle); border-color: var(--bn-primary); color: var(--bn-primary); }
.bn-hamburger { display: inline-flex; }
@media (min-width: 860px) { .bn-hamburger { display: none; } }
.bn-mobile-nav { position: fixed; inset: 0 0 auto 0; top: var(--bn-header-height); background: var(--bn-surface); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--bn-border); box-shadow: var(--bn-shadow-3); z-index: var(--bn-z-dropdown); padding: var(--bn-space-4) var(--bn-space-6) var(--bn-space-6); transform: translateY(-8px); opacity: 0; pointer-events: none; transition: transform var(--bn-transition-base), opacity var(--bn-transition-base); }
.bn-mobile-nav.is-open { transform: translateY(0); opacity: 1; pointer-events: auto; }
.bn-mobile-nav a { display: block; padding: var(--bn-space-3) 0; font-weight: var(--bn-fw-medium); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--bn-border); color: var(--bn-text-primary); }
.bn-mobile-nav a[aria-current="page"] { color: var(--bn-primary); font-weight: var(--bn-fw-semibold); }
@media (min-width: 860px) { .bn-mobile-nav { display: none; } }
.bn-scroll-locked { overflow: hidden; }
.bn-nav-overlay { position: fixed; inset: 0; background: hsla(220, 24%, 12%, 0.45); opacity: 0; pointer-events: none; z-index: var(--bn-z-dropdown); transition: opacity var(--bn-transition-base); }
.bn-nav-overlay.is-open { opacity: 1; pointer-events: auto; }

/* --- Main --- */
.bn-main { min-height: 60vh; }

/* --- Footer --- */
.bn-footer { border-top: 1px solid var(--bn-border); padding-block: var(--bn-space-12) var(--bn-space-8); background: var(--bn-surface); }
.bn-footer-grid { display: grid; gap: var(--bn-space-8); grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; }
@media (min-width: 760px) { .bn-footer-grid { grid-template-columns: 1.4fr repeat(3, 1fr); } }
.bn-footer-tagline { color: var(--bn-text-secondary); font-size: var(--bn-fs-sm); max-width: 32ch; margin-top: var(--bn-space-3); }
.bn-footer-heading { font-size: var(--bn-fs-sm); font-weight: var(--bn-fw-semibold); margin-bottom: var(--bn-space-3); color: var(--bn-text-primary); }
.bn-footer-links li { margin-bottom: var(--bn-space-2); }
.bn-footer-links a { font-size: var(--bn-fs-sm); color: var(--bn-text-secondary); }
.bn-footer-links a:hover { color: var(--bn-primary); }
.bn-footer-bottom { margin-top: var(--bn-space-10); padding-top: var(--bn-space-6); border-top: 1px solid var(--bn-border); display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: var(--bn-space-4); align-items: center; justify-content: space-between; font-size: var(--bn-fs-xs); color: var(--bn-text-tertiary); }
.bn-footer-bottom a { color: var(--bn-text-tertiary); text-decoration: underline; }
.bn-footer-bottom a:hover { color: var(--bn-primary); }

/* --- Post / Tool Page shell (extended by the Universal Tool Template, Roadmap Step 4) --- */
.bn-tool-page { max-width: var(--bn-content-max); margin-inline: auto; padding-block: var(--bn-space-12); }
.bn-tool-page :is(h2, h3) { margin-top: var(--bn-space-8); margin-bottom: var(--bn-space-3); }
.bn-tool-page p { margin-bottom: var(--bn-space-4); line-height: var(--bn-lh-relaxed); }

/* ==========================================================================
   6. UTILITY CLASSES
   ========================================================================== */
.bn-visually-hidden { position: absolute; width: 1px; height: 1px; padding: 0; margin: -1px; overflow: hidden; clip: rect(0,0,0,0); white-space: nowrap; border: 0; }
.u-text-center { text-align: center; }
.u-text-left { text-align: left; }
.u-text-right { text-align: right; }
.u-flex { display: flex; }
.u-grid { display: grid; }
.u-items-center { align-items: center; }
.u-justify-between { justify-content: space-between; }
.u-gap-2 { gap: var(--bn-space-2); }
.u-gap-4 { gap: var(--bn-space-4); }
.u-gap-6 { gap: var(--bn-space-6); }
.u-mt-2 { margin-top: var(--bn-space-2); } .u-mt-4 { margin-top: var(--bn-space-4); } .u-mt-8 { margin-top: var(--bn-space-8); }
.u-mb-2 { margin-bottom: var(--bn-space-2); } .u-mb-4 { margin-bottom: var(--bn-space-4); } .u-mb-8 { margin-bottom: var(--bn-space-8); }
.u-p-4 { padding: var(--bn-space-4); } .u-p-6 { padding: var(--bn-space-6); }
.u-hide-mobile { display: none; }
@media (min-width: 640px) { .u-hide-mobile { display: revert; } .u-hide-desktop { display: none; } }
/* Reserved for large future directories (Homepage/Tool Directory grids) per Part 4 Section 20 — apply selectively, not globally */
.u-cv-auto { content-visibility: auto; contain-intrinsic-size: 600px; }

/* ==========================================================================
   7. RESPONSIVE (global overrides; component-level breakpoints live inline
   above within their own component block — see Design_System_v1.0.md
   Section 8 for the full breakpoint list)
   ========================================================================== */
@media (min-width: 640px) {
  h1 { font-size: var(--bn-fs-4xl); }
  .bn-section { padding-block: var(--bn-space-16); }
}

/* ==========================================================================
   8. PRINT STYLES
   ========================================================================== */
@media print {
  .bn-header, .bn-footer, .bn-mobile-nav, .bn-nav-overlay, .bn-skip-link, .bn-icon-btn, script { display: none !important; }
  body { background: #fff; color: #000; }
  .bn-tool-page { max-width: 100%; }
  a[href]::after { content: " (" attr(href) ")"; font-size: 0.85em; color: #555; }
}

]]></b:skin>
</head>
<body>
<a class='bn-skip-link' href='#main-content'>Skip to content</a>

<!-- Global live region for screen-reader announcements (Banynova.a11y.announce uses this) -->
<div aria-live='polite' class='bn-visually-hidden' id='bn-live-region'></div>

<!-- Shared SVG symbol sprite — the logo is defined once and referenced via
     <use> in the header and footer, per Part 2 Section 16. Visually hidden;
     not a rendering target itself. -->
<svg aria-hidden='true' class='bn-visually-hidden'>
  <symbol id='bn-logo-icon' viewBox='0 0 24 24'>
    <rect height='18' rx='5' stroke='currentColor' stroke-width='2' width='18' x='3' y='3'></rect>
    <path d='M8 12h5m0 0-2-2m2 2-2 2' stroke='currentColor' stroke-linecap='round' stroke-linejoin='round' stroke-width='2'></path>
  </symbol>
</svg>

<!-- ============================== HEADER ============================== -->
<b:section id='bn-header-section' maxwidgets='1' name='Header' showaddelement='no'>
<b:widget id='Header1' locked='true' title='Banynova' type='Header' version='2'>
<b:includable id='main'>
<header class='bn-header' id='bn-header'>
  <div class='bn-container bn-header-inner'>
    <a class='bn-logo' expr:href='data:blog.homepageUrl'>
      <svg class='bn-logo-mark' height='26' width='26'><use href='#bn-logo-icon'></use></svg>
      <data:blog.title/>
    </a>
    <nav aria-label='Primary Navigation' class='bn-nav' id='bn-nav-primary'>
      <a expr:href='data:blog.homepageUrl'>Tools</a>
      <a expr:href='data:blog.homepageUrl + &quot;p/categories.html&quot;'>Categories</a>
      <a expr:href='data:blog.homepageUrl + &quot;p/blog.html&quot;'>Blog</a>
      <a expr:href='data:blog.homepageUrl + &quot;p/resources.html&quot;'>Resources</a>
      <a expr:href='data:blog.homepageUrl + &quot;p/about.html&quot;'>About</a>
    </nav>
    <div class='bn-header-actions'>
      <button aria-label='Toggle dark mode' aria-pressed='false' class='bn-icon-btn' id='bn-theme-toggle' type='button'>
        <svg height='18' id='bn-theme-icon' viewBox='0 0 24 24' width='18'><circle cx='12' cy='12' r='4' stroke='currentColor' stroke-width='2'></circle><path d='M12 2v2M12 20v2M4.9 4.9l1.4 1.4M17.7 17.7l1.4 1.4M2 12h2M20 12h2M4.9 19.1l1.4-1.4M17.7 6.3l1.4-1.4' stroke='currentColor' stroke-linecap='round' stroke-width='2'></path></svg>
      </button>
      <button aria-expanded='false' aria-label='Open menu' class='bn-icon-btn bn-hamburger' id='bn-menu-toggle' type='button'>
        <svg height='18' viewBox='0 0 24 24' width='18'><path d='M4 7h16M4 12h16M4 17h16' stroke='currentColor' stroke-linecap='round' stroke-width='2'></path></svg>
      </button>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class='bn-nav-overlay' id='bn-nav-overlay'></div>
  <nav aria-label='Mobile Navigation' class='bn-mobile-nav' id='bn-mobile-nav'>
    <a expr:href='data:blog.homepageUrl'>Tools</a>
    <a expr:href='data:blog.homepageUrl + &quot;p/categories.html&quot;'>Categories</a>
    <a expr:href='data:blog.homepageUrl + &quot;p/blog.html&quot;'>Blog</a>
    <a expr:href='data:blog.homepageUrl + &quot;p/resources.html&quot;'>Resources</a>
    <a expr:href='data:blog.homepageUrl + &quot;p/about.html&quot;'>About</a>
  </nav>
</header>
</b:includable>
</b:widget>
</b:section>

<!-- ============================== MAIN ============================== -->
<main class='bn-main' id='main-content'>
<b:section id='bn-main-section' name='Main' showaddelement='yes'>
<b:widget id='Blog1' locked='true' title='Blog Posts' type='Blog' version='2'>
<b:includable id='main'>
<b:if cond='data:blog.url == data:blog.homepageUrl'>
  <!-- Homepage v1.x injects here -->
<b:else/>
  <b:loop values='data:posts' var='post'>
    <b:include data='post' name='post'/>
  </b:loop>
</b:if>
</b:includable>
<b:includable id='post' var='post'>
<article class='bn-tool-page'>
  <h1><data:post.title/></h1>
  <data:post.body/>
</article>
</b:includable>
</b:widget>
</b:section>
</main>

<!-- ============================== FOOTER ============================== -->
<footer class='bn-footer'>
<div class='bn-container bn-footer-grid'>
  <div>
    <a class='bn-logo' expr:href='data:blog.homepageUrl'>
      <svg class='bn-logo-mark' height='24' width='24'><use href='#bn-logo-icon'></use></svg>
      <data:blog.title/>
    </a>
    <p class='bn-footer-tagline'>Powering Your Digital Workflow. Built for developers, creators, marketers, students, and everyone in between.</p>
  </div>
  <div>
    <h3 class='bn-footer-heading'>Quick Links</h3>
    <ul class='bn-footer-links'>
      <li><a expr:href='data:blog.homepageUrl + &quot;p/categories.html&quot;'>Categories</a></li>
      <li><a expr:href='data:blog.homepageUrl + &quot;p/blog.html&quot;'>Blog</a></li>
      <li><a expr:href='data:blog.homepageUrl + &quot;p/resources.html&quot;'>Resources</a></li>
      <li><a expr:href='data:blog.homepageUrl + &quot;sitemap.xml&quot;'>Sitemap</a></li>
      <li><a expr:href='data:blog.homepageUrl + &quot;feeds/posts/default&quot;'>RSS Feed</a></li>
    </ul>
  </div>
  <div>
    <h3 class='bn-footer-heading'>Legal</h3>
    <ul class='bn-footer-links'>
      <li><a expr:href='data:blog.homepageUrl + &quot;p/privacy-policy.html&quot;'>Privacy Policy</a></li>
      <li><a expr:href='data:blog.homepageUrl + &quot;p/terms.html&quot;'>Terms of Service</a></li>
      <li><a expr:href='data:blog.homepageUrl + &quot;p/cookies.html&quot;'>Cookies</a></li>
      <li><a expr:href='data:blog.homepageUrl + &quot;p/accessibility.html&quot;'>Accessibility</a></li>
    </ul>
  </div>
  <div>
    <h3 class='bn-footer-heading'>Contact</h3>
    <ul class='bn-footer-links'>
      <li><a expr:href='data:blog.homepageUrl + &quot;p/contact.html&quot;'>Contact Us</a></li>
      <!-- Replace # with the real GitHub org URL once created -->
      <li><a href='#'>GitHub</a></li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</div>
<b:section id='bn-footer-section' name='Footer' showaddelement='yes'>
</b:section>
<div class='bn-container bn-footer-bottom'>
  <span>© <span id='bn-year'></span> Banynova. All rights reserved. <a expr:href='data:blog.homepageUrl + &quot;p/disclaimer.html&quot;'>Disclaimer</a></span>
  <span>Your files never leave your browser.</span>
</div>
</footer>

<!-- ============================== BASE JAVASCRIPT ============================== -->
<script>//<![CDATA[
(function (global) {
  'use strict';

  var Banynova = global.Banynova || {};

  /* ------------------------------------------------------------------------
     MODULE REGISTRATION — the one sanctioned way to add a module to the
     Banynova namespace, now or in any future tool script. Because each
     module is frozen individually (never the top-level Banynova object —
     see the reasoning at the bottom of this file), a future script must
     never write `Banynova.search = {...}` directly for an existing name,
     and never mutate an already-registered module's properties after the
     fact. Banynova.register() enforces both: it refuses to silently
     overwrite an existing module (warns instead), and freezes whatever it
     registers immediately, so every module — this file's or a future
     tool's — ends up equally protected without each script having to
     remember to call Object.freeze itself.
     Usage from a future tool page: Banynova.register('search', { ... });
     ------------------------------------------------------------------------ */
  Object.defineProperty(Banynova, 'register', {
    value: function (name, module) {
      if (Object.prototype.hasOwnProperty.call(Banynova, name)) {
        if (window.console && console.warn) {
          console.warn('Banynova.register: "' + name + '" already exists and was not overwritten. Choose a different module name.');
        }
        return Banynova[name];
      }
      Banynova[name] = module;
      if (Object.freeze) { Object.freeze(module); }
      return module;
    },
    writable: false,
    configurable: false,
    enumerable: true
  });

  /* ------------------------------------------------------------------------
     STORAGE — thin, safe wrapper (private browsing / disabled storage
     should never throw and break the page)
     ------------------------------------------------------------------------ */
  Banynova.register('storage', {
    get: function (key) {
      try { return window.localStorage.getItem(key); } catch (e) { return null; }
    },
    set: function (key, value) {
      try { window.localStorage.setItem(key, value); return true; } catch (e) { return false; }
    },
    remove: function (key) {
      try { window.localStorage.removeItem(key); return true; } catch (e) { return false; }
    }
  });

  /* ------------------------------------------------------------------------
     THEME TOGGLE SYSTEM
     ------------------------------------------------------------------------ */
  Banynova.register('theme', {
    STORAGE_KEY: 'bn-theme',
    // Static, hardcoded icon markup (no user input involved) — safe to set
    // via innerHTML per Part 5 Section 23; never used with dynamic data.
    ICON_SUN: '<circle cx="12" cy="12" r="4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"></circle><path d="M12 2v2M12 20v2M4.9 4.9l1.4 1.4M17.7 17.7l1.4 1.4M2 12h2M20 12h2M4.9 19.1l1.4-1.4M17.7 6.3l1.4-1.4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-width="2"></path>',
    ICON_MOON: '<path d="M21 12.79A9 9 0 1 1 11.21 3 7 7 0 0 0 21 12.79z" stroke="currentColor" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2"></path>',
    get: function () {
      return document.documentElement.getAttribute('data-theme') || 'light';
    },
    set: function (mode) {
      document.documentElement.setAttribute('data-theme', mode);
      Banynova.storage.set(this.STORAGE_KEY, mode);
    },
    toggle: function () {
      this.set(this.get() === 'dark' ? 'light' : 'dark');
    },
    init: function () {
      var toggle = document.getElementById('bn-theme-toggle');
      var icon = document.getElementById('bn-theme-icon');
      if (!toggle) { return; }
      function updateThemeButton(announce) {
        var dark = Banynova.theme.get() === 'dark';
        toggle.setAttribute('aria-pressed', String(dark));
        toggle.setAttribute('aria-label', dark ? 'Switch to light mode' : 'Switch to dark mode');
        if (icon) { icon.innerHTML = dark ? Banynova.theme.ICON_MOON : Banynova.theme.ICON_SUN; }
        if (announce) { Banynova.a11y.announce(dark ? 'Dark mode enabled' : 'Light mode enabled'); }
      }
      updateThemeButton(false);
      toggle.addEventListener('click', function () {
        Banynova.theme.toggle();
        updateThemeButton(true);
      });
    }
  });

  /* ------------------------------------------------------------------------
     ACCESSIBILITY HELPERS
     ------------------------------------------------------------------------ */
  Banynova.register('a11y', {
    announce: function (message) {
      var region = document.getElementById('bn-live-region');
      if (!region) { return; }
      region.textContent = '';
      window.setTimeout(function () { region.textContent = message; }, 50);
    },
    prefersReducedMotion: function () {
      return !!(window.matchMedia && window.matchMedia('(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)').matches);
    },
    trapFocus: function (container) {
      var focusable = container.querySelectorAll('a[href], button:not([disabled]), input, select, textarea, [tabindex]:not([tabindex="-1"])');
      if (focusable.length === 0) { return function () {}; }
      var first = focusable[0];
      var last = focusable[focusable.length - 1];
      function handleKey(e) {
        if (e.key !== 'Tab') { return; }
        if (e.shiftKey && document.activeElement === first) { e.preventDefault(); last.focus(); }
        else if (!e.shiftKey && document.activeElement === last) { e.preventDefault(); first.focus(); }
      }
      container.addEventListener('keydown', handleKey);
      return function () { container.removeEventListener('keydown', handleKey); };
    }
  });

  /* ------------------------------------------------------------------------
     GLOBAL UTILITIES
     ------------------------------------------------------------------------ */
  Banynova.register('utils', {
    qs: function (sel, ctx) { return (ctx || document).querySelector(sel); },
    qsa: function (sel, ctx) { return Array.prototype.slice.call((ctx || document).querySelectorAll(sel)); },
    debounce: function (fn, wait) {
      var t;
      return function () {
        var args = arguments, ctx = this;
        window.clearTimeout(t);
        t = window.setTimeout(function () { fn.apply(ctx, args); }, wait || 250);
      };
    },
    throttle: function (fn, limit) {
      var inThrottle;
      return function () {
        var args = arguments, ctx = this;
        if (!inThrottle) {
          fn.apply(ctx, args);
          inThrottle = true;
          window.setTimeout(function () { inThrottle = false; }, limit || 100);
        }
      };
    }
  });

  /* ------------------------------------------------------------------------
     PERFORMANCE HELPERS
     ------------------------------------------------------------------------ */
  Banynova.register('perf', {
    lazyLoadImages: function (selector) {
      var imgs = Banynova.utils.qsa(selector || 'img[data-src]');
      if (imgs.length === 0) { return; }
      if (!('IntersectionObserver' in window)) {
        imgs.forEach(function (img) { img.src = img.getAttribute('data-src'); });
        return;
      }
      var observer = new IntersectionObserver(function (entries, obs) {
        entries.forEach(function (entry) {
          if (entry.isIntersecting) {
            var img = entry.target;
            img.src = img.getAttribute('data-src');
            img.removeAttribute('data-src');
            obs.unobserve(img);
          }
        });
      });
      imgs.forEach(function (img) { observer.observe(img); });
    },
    // Blogger post-body <img> tags come from user-authored content and
    // can't be templated directly. This applies Part 2 Section 15's
    // loading="lazy" / decoding="async" rule after the fact, skipping the
    // first image in the post so a genuine hero/LCP image is never
    // lazy-loaded (Part 8 Section 14).
    applyLazyLoadingToPostImages: function () {
      var imgs = Banynova.utils.qsa('.bn-tool-page img');
      imgs.forEach(function (img, index) {
        if (index === 0) { return; }
        if (!img.hasAttribute('loading')) { img.setAttribute('loading', 'lazy'); }
        if (!img.hasAttribute('decoding')) { img.setAttribute('decoding', 'async'); }
      });
    },
    loadScript: function (src, callback) {
      var existing = document.querySelector('script[src="' + src + '"]');
      if (existing) { if (callback) { callback(); } return; }
      var s = document.createElement('script');
      s.src = src;
      s.async = true;
      if (callback) { s.onload = callback; }
      document.head.appendChild(s);
    }
  });

  /* ------------------------------------------------------------------------
     BROWSER COMPATIBILITY / FEATURE SUPPORT
     ------------------------------------------------------------------------ */
  Banynova.register('support', {
    clipboard: !!(navigator.clipboard && navigator.clipboard.writeText),
    webCrypto: !!(window.crypto && window.crypto.subtle),
    intersectionObserver: 'IntersectionObserver' in window,
    backdropFilter: !!(window.CSS && window.CSS.supports && (window.CSS.supports('backdrop-filter', 'blur(1px)') || window.CSS.supports('-webkit-backdrop-filter', 'blur(1px)')))
  });

  /* ------------------------------------------------------------------------
     NAVIGATION MODULE — header scroll effect, mobile menu, active link.
     Matches the Module Architecture in Part 5 Section 4 (one module, one
     responsibility). Scroll handler is throttled per Part 5 Section 12 /
     Part 8 Section 21, never left unthrottled.
     ------------------------------------------------------------------------ */
  Banynova.register('navigation', {
    initScrollEffect: function () {
      var header = document.getElementById('bn-header');
      if (!header) { return; }
      var onScroll = Banynova.utils.throttle(function () {
        header.classList.toggle('is-scrolled', window.scrollY > 8);
      }, 100);
      window.addEventListener('scroll', onScroll, { passive: true });
    },
    initMobileMenu: function () {
      var menuBtn = document.getElementById('bn-menu-toggle');
      var mobileNav = document.getElementById('bn-mobile-nav');
      var overlay = document.getElementById('bn-nav-overlay');
      if (!menuBtn || !mobileNav) { return; }
      var releaseFocusTrap = null;
      function openMenu() {
        mobileNav.classList.add('is-open');
        menuBtn.setAttribute('aria-expanded', 'true');
        document.body.classList.add('bn-scroll-locked');
        if (overlay) { overlay.classList.add('is-open'); }
        releaseFocusTrap = Banynova.a11y.trapFocus(mobileNav);
      }
      function closeMenu() {
        mobileNav.classList.remove('is-open');
        menuBtn.setAttribute('aria-expanded', 'false');
        document.body.classList.remove('bn-scroll-locked');
        if (overlay) { overlay.classList.remove('is-open'); }
        if (releaseFocusTrap) { releaseFocusTrap(); releaseFocusTrap = null; }
      }
      menuBtn.addEventListener('click', function (e) {
        e.stopPropagation();
        if (mobileNav.classList.contains('is-open')) { closeMenu(); } else { openMenu(); }
      });
      if (overlay) {
        overlay.addEventListener('click', function () { closeMenu(); menuBtn.focus(); });
      }
      document.addEventListener('click', function (e) {
        if (mobileNav.classList.contains('is-open') && !mobileNav.contains(e.target) && !menuBtn.contains(e.target)) {
          closeMenu();
        }
      });
      document.addEventListener('keydown', function (e) {
        if (e.key === 'Escape' && mobileNav.classList.contains('is-open')) {
          closeMenu();
          menuBtn.focus();
        }
      });
    },
    // Marks the nav link matching the current page with aria-current="page"
    // (Part 3 Section 8 / Part 6 Section 5). Strips hash, query params
    // (e.g. Blogger's ?m=1 mobile param), and trailing slashes before
    // comparing, so "banynova.blogspot.com/" and "banynova.blogspot.com"
    // are treated as the same URL. Safe no-op until the linked pages
    // actually exist — matches nothing rather than matching wrong.
    normalizeUrl: function (url) {
      return url.split('#')[0].split('?')[0].replace(/\/+$/, '');
    },
    initActiveLink: function () {
      var here = Banynova.navigation.normalizeUrl(window.location.href);
      Banynova.utils.qsa('#bn-nav-primary a, #bn-mobile-nav a').forEach(function (link) {
        var target = Banynova.navigation.normalizeUrl(link.href);
        if (target === here) { link.setAttribute('aria-current', 'page'); }
      });
    },
    init: function () {
      this.initScrollEffect();
      this.initMobileMenu();
      this.initActiveLink();
      var yearEl = document.getElementById('bn-year');
      if (yearEl) { yearEl.textContent = String(new Date().getFullYear()); }
    }
  });

  global.Banynova = Banynova;

  // Each module above was already frozen individually by Banynova.register()
  // as it was added — see that function's comment near the top of this
  // script for the full reasoning (deliberately not freezing the top-level
  // Banynova object itself, so future tool pages can still add new
  // modules via Banynova.register('search', {...}), etc.).

  Banynova.theme.init();
  Banynova.navigation.init();
  Banynova.perf.applyLazyLoadingToPostImages();

})(window);
//]]></script>

</body>
</html>
